<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">France Prešeren</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800–1849</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> Prešeren was a Romantic poet and the national poet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>. A lawyer who worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ljubljana">Ljubljana</a> and Kranj, he wrote in Slovene when German dominated educated life, and his collected Poems and the epic 'The Baptism on the Savica' raised Slovene literature to a European level. A stanza of his poem 'A Toast' is the national anthem of Slovenia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france-preseren.jpg" alt="France Prešeren" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz von Kurz zum Thurn und Goldenstein · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pre%C5%A1ern-Goldenstein.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
